992: ### Using the prefix option
993: 
994: If your project has class names that conflict with Tailwind CSS utilities, you can prefix all Tailwind-generated classes and CSS variables using the `prefix` option:
995: 
996: <CodeExampleStack>
997: 
998: ```css
999: /* [!code filename:app.css] */
1000: /* [!code word:important] */
1001: @import "tailwindcss" prefix(tw);
1002: ```
1003: 
1004: ```css
1005: /* [!code filename:Compiled CSS] */
1006: /* [!code word:tw\:] */
1007: @layer theme {
1008:   :root {
1009:     --tw-color-red-500: oklch(0.637 0.237 25.331);
1010:   }
1011: }
1012: 
1013: @layer utilities {
1014:   .tw\:text-red-500 {
1015:     color: var(--tw-color-red-500);
1016:   }
1017: }
1018: ```
